Step 4: Since the problem states \(\overline{XM}\parallel \overline{AC}\) and from Step 2 we have \(X=(2,0)\) while \(AC\) is the segment from \(A=(0,0)\) to \(C=\left(\tfrac12,\tfrac{7\sqrt3}{2}\right)\), the direction vector of \(AC\) is \(\left(\tfrac12,\tfrac{7\sqrt3}{2}\right)\); thus the line through \(X\) parallel to \(AC\) has parametric form \( (x,y)=\left(2,0\right)+t\left(\tfrac12,\tfrac{7\sqrt3}{2}\right)\), so \(y= t\cdot \tfrac{7\sqrt3}{2}\) and the slope equals \(\dfrac{(7\sqrt3/2)}{(1/2)}=7\sqrt3\). Intersecting this with side \(BC\), whose line through \(B=(5,0)\) and \(C=\left(\tfrac12,\tfrac{7\sqrt3}{2}\right)\) is \( (x,y)=\left(5,0\right)+r\left(-\tfrac{9}{2},\tfrac{7\sqrt3}{2}\right)\), gives \(\tfrac{7\sqrt3}{2}t=\tfrac{7\sqrt3}{2}r\Rightarrow t=r\) and \(2+\tfrac12 t=5-\tfrac{9}{2}t\), so \( \tfrac12 t+\tfrac{9}{2}t=3\Rightarrow 5t=3\Rightarrow t=\tfrac{3}{5}\), hence \(M=\left(2+\tfrac12\cdot\tfrac35,\ 0+\tfrac{7\sqrt3}{2}\cdot\tfrac35\right)=\left(\tfrac{13}{10},\ \tfrac{21\sqrt3}{10}\right)\).
